  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  # Delete Booking

  Permanently deletes a booking record.

  ## URL Parameters
  - `booking_id`: The ID of the booking to delete

  ## Important Notes
  - This is a **hard delete** (permanent removal)
  - Cannot be undone
  - Use with caution
  - Associated activity (if any) is NOT deleted

  ## Response
  - Status: 204 No Content (success)
  - Empty response body

  ## When to Delete vs Cancel

  **Delete** when:
  - Duplicate booking entry
  - Entered wrong information
  - Testing/development data
  - Booking never actually existed

  **Cancel** (use Update instead) when:
  - Legitimate booking that was cancelled
  - Want to keep history
  - May need to reference later
  - Track cancellations

  ## Recommended: Cancel Instead
  ```
  PUT /api/v1/bookings/{booking_id}
  {
    "status": "cancelled",
    "notes": "Cancelled on 2025-01-02. Refund: ¥45,000"
  }
  ```

  ## Access Control
  - Requires authentication
  - User must own the trip
  - Returns 403 Forbidden if unauthorized
  - Returns 404 Not Found if booking doesn't exist

  ## Cascade Effects
  - Booking is removed from database
  - Associated activity remains intact
  - Associated trip day remains intact
  - No other bookings are affected
}
